  "result": "Perfect! All 171 tests pass (162 original + 9 new payment terms tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n\u2705 **Added payment terms support to `createInvoice`**\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter: 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM'\n- Defaults to 'NET30' if not specified\n- Sets both `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate`\n\n\u2705 **Created `calculateDueDate` helper function**\n- **NET14**: due 14 days after issue date (via `addDays`)\n- **NET30**: due 30 days after issue date (via `addDays`)\n- **EOM**: due on the last day of the issue date's month\n  - Handles leap years correctly (Feb 29 for 2024, Feb 28 for 2025)\n  - Works by using JavaScript's UTC date to find the last day\n\n\u2705 **Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code** to `src/errors.js`\n- Triggered when an unknown term is provided\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (9 new) covering:\n- Default NET30 behavior\n- Explicit NET14 terms\n- Explicit NET30 terms\n- EOM terms (various months)\n- Leap year EOM calculation (Feb 29)\n- Invalid terms error handling\n- Month boundary handling (NET14/NET30 rolling into next month)\n\n\u2705 **All house rules followed:**\n- No mutations\n- Tests pass\n- Integrated with existing date utilities (`addDays`)",
